{"term":"branch","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:b9945e4fb28b84a1ba","definition":"The woody part of a tree arising from the trunk and usually dividing.","example":"Selfe loue, to him ſelf tender, to the reſt tough, / Is, of iuſt iuſtice, neither roote, braunce, nor bough. / Loue (namely ſelfe loue) corruptibly growyng, / Is cheefe lodeſter of lets, in iuſtice ſhowing.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["arm","bough","grain","limb","tiller","tillow","twig","tree"],"antonyms":["crotch"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["branched","branchery","branchful","branchless","branchlet","branchlike","branchling","branchwise","branchwork","branchy","The Branch"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/branch#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d51287cf21e710eda2","definition":"Any of the parts of something that divides like the branch of a tree.","example":"the branch of an antler, a chandelier, or a railway","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["crotch"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["branched","branchery","branchful","branchless","branchlet","branchlike","branchling","branchwise","branchwork","branchy","The Branch"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/branch#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2bedb51fe524514df6","definition":"A creek or stream which flows into a larger river.","example":"branch water","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["crotch"],"collocations":[],"usage":"Southern-US","register":"Southern-US","wordFamily":["branched","branchery","branchful","branchless","branchlet","branchlike","branchling","branchwise","branchwork","branchy","The Branch"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/branch#English","license